<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kandariya Mahadeva Temple</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1030</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kandariya Mahadeva Temple is the largest and most elaborate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> temple at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khajuraho">Khajuraho</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, built around 1030 under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandela-dynasty">Chandela dynasty</a> and dedicated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiva">Shiva</a>. Its soaring spire of 84 miniature towers and its hundreds of finely carved figures, including erotic sculptures, make it a masterpiece of the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bednur">Nagara</a> style.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kandariya-mahadeva-temple.jpg" alt="Kandariya Mahadeva Temple" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: China Crisis · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khajuraho.KandariyaMahadeva.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
